/**
 * Golden values of TFC's cluster veins at the pinned commit (c3b4d9536), for the 33 cluster vein types of the shipped data.
 *
 * <p>The expected values came from TFC's own classes: {@code VeinFeature}, {@code ClusterVeinFeature}, {@code ClusterVeinConfig},
 * {@code IVeinConfig}, {@code VeinConfig} (its codec removed, {@code hash} kept), {@code Metaballs3D}, {@code Weighted} and
 * {@code IWeighted}, compiled against Minecraft 1.21.11's own {@code RandomSource}, {@code XoroshiroRandomSource},
 * {@code Xoroshiro128PlusPlus} and {@code RandomSupport} (the 1.21 {@code nextDouble} that goes through a float, as TFC's 1.21.1
 * runs it; 26.3's is full precision and gives other balls) and DataFixerUpper's {@code Pair}, with stubs for {@code BlockPos}, {@code BoundingBox},
 * {@code WorldGenLevel} and the block types. The vein JSON was TFC's {@code data/tfc/worldgen/configured_feature/vein/}. Nothing
 * was run on a server.
 * <ul>
 *   <li>{@link #SEEDS}: {@code VeinConfig.hash(random_name)} of every type.</li>
 *   <li>{@link #VEINS}: {@code getVeinsAtChunk} over chunks x, z in [-8, 7] (x outer): the vein count, an FNV-style hash of
 *       each vein's chunk, centre and balls (the record text of each {@code Metaballs3D.Ball}), and the first vein written out.</li>
 *   <li>{@link #MASKS}: TFC's {@code VeinFeature.place} for six chunks (including negative ones), in a level that is the type's
 *       first replaced rock everywhere and a random whose {@code nextFloat} is always 0 (every roll inside the shape passes): the
 *       number of {@code setBlock} calls and a hash of their positions in call order. This is the exact shape, centre, box and
 *       height clamp.</li>
 *   <li>{@link #PICKS}: {@code IWeighted.get((k + 0.5) / 32)} for k = 0..31 on the type's first rock entry, as the index of the
 *       picked block in the list's values.</li>
 * </ul>
 */
